#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:10
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:12
msgid ""
"Define the **shared 6-tier size ladder** that lives in `size:` "
"frontmatter on every sized spec, and the **nudge protocol** delivery "
"leads follow when they encounter an oversized one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:16
msgid "Two jobs:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:17
msgid ""
"Tell a lead what a `size:` value means (and what the spec writer probably"
" meant by choosing it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:19
msgid ""
"Tell a lead exactly what to say, when, and how loud — so the same nudge "
"fires consistently across sessions, agents, and trackers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"This skill is **the source of truth**. The delivery leads reference it; "
"the CLI (`hero size`, `hero sprint estimate`, `hero check`, "
"`hero_warnings`) implements the mechanics. The nudge text below is paste-"
"ready — leads quote it directly so wording stays consistent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:27
msgid "When to use me"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"**Design time** — when authoring a new spec via `/design`, stamp `size:` "
"based on the design conversation. Default to `medium` only when truly "
"undetermined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:32
msgid ""
"**Delivery pickup** — when starting `/deliver` on a spec, read its "
"`size:` and `size_ack:`, run `hero size --check`, and fire the "
"appropriate nudge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:35
msgid ""
"**Mid-delivery** — if scope grows or drift surfaces, bump declared "
"`size:` via `hero size <slug> <tier>` instead of ignoring."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:38
msgid "The ladder"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:40
msgid ""
"One vocabulary across all sized spec types. Each tier represents roughly "
"the same **absolute magnitude of effort**, regardless of which type "
"carries it. What's \"normal\" for an initiative is alarming for a feature"
" — that's what the per-type bands below capture."
msgstr ""

