#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "re-recommend each time"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "strong rec every session until ack, split, or scope shrinks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:84
msgid "Tracker-aware tuning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:86
msgid ""
"The threshold at which the nudge fires shifts based on what the tracker "
"can do for hierarchy. Read `hero.json: tracker.type` and the adapter's "
"`supports_hierarchy` flag (slice 5 wires the adapter side; until then "
"default to \"no tracker\" behavior)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "Regime"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "Nudge schedule"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "Promotion offered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "**No tracker** (`type: \"none\"`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Most aggressive: `large` → soft, `x-large` → strong, `giant` → super-"
"strong"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Local promotion only — turn this spec into an initiative with children in"
" `.hero/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "**Tracker without hierarchy** (basic GitHub issues, flat Linear, etc.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "Same as no-tracker"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Local promotion only — Hero handles parent/child locally; the tracker "
"just sees the child issues."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"**Tracker with strong hierarchy** (Jira epics, Linear projects, GitHub "
"sub-issues)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid "Less aggressive: soft starts at `x-large`, strong at `giant`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md
msgid ""
"Promotion offers to **create the parent in the tracker too**, so the "
"human team's view stays coherent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:97
msgid "The acknowledgement protocol"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:99
msgid ""
"`size_ack:` has two jobs. Both come down to the same principle: when "
"someone inspected the actual work and concluded the declared tier is "
"right, the system should stop arguing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:103
msgid "Job 1 — suppress the `giant` design-time nudge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:105
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: ...\n"
"type: feature\n"
"size: giant\n"
"size_ack: giant\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:114
msgid ""
"`size_ack: giant` says \"yes, I know it's giant, I'm shipping it as one "
"spec anyway.\" Suppresses the super-strong design-time recommendation to "
"`/compose`. **Does not** suppress mid-delivery surfacing — every delivery"
" session on a `giant` spec still gets the strong rec, because that's "
"where the size is being felt."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:120
msgid "Job 2 — inspector wins over the computed heuristic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:122
msgid ""
"---\n"
"title: ...\n"
"type: feature\n"
"size: medium\n"
"size_ack: medium\n"
"---\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:131
msgid ""
"When `size_ack:` matches the declared `size:`, the drift detector treats "
"it as \"the work was inspected; declared stands.\" Suppresses the drift "
"warning even when `hero sprint estimate`'s computed bucket disagrees. "
"This is the **inspector-wins rule**: the person who looked at the actual "
"implementation outranks a word-count heuristic that only inspected the "
"spec body."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:138
msgid "When to use it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:139
msgid ""
"A `/roadmap-review` session walked the drift and the user/agent confirmed"
" declared is right (prose-dense specs that compute high, structured-data-"
"dense specs that compute low)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:142
msgid ""
"A delivery-lead audit confirmed the spec scope matches declared after "
"delivery — agent acks before flipping `status: completed`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:145
msgid "When NOT to use it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:146
msgid ""
"Just to silence drift you haven't actually inspected. Acking without "
"thinking is the same anti-pattern as marking a ticket `won't-fix` to "
"clear a queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:150
msgid "Rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:152
msgid ""
"The user, or an agent that just inspected the work, decides to set "
"`size_ack`. The lead asks; the lead does not auto-stamp on a spec it "
"hasn't read."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:155
msgid ""
"**Stale acks are ignored.** If you bump declared (`size: medium → large`)"
" but the ack stays at the old value (`size_ack: medium`), the drift "
"detector treats the ack as stale and re-fires. Update the ack or drop it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:159
msgid "If the spec is split or scope shrinks, drop the `size_ack` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:160
msgid ""
"The `roadmap-reviewer` agent should ack every \"keep declared as-is\" "
"decision in its session — that's the durable record of inspection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:163
msgid "Drift handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:165
msgid ""
"When `hero size --check`, `hero check`, or `hero_warnings` surfaces drift"
" between declared and computed size, the lead does **not** ignore it. Two"
" flavors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:169
msgid ""
"**Leaf drift** (feature/bug/enhancement): declared `size:` differs from "
"`hero sprint estimate` bucket. Bump declared via `hero size <slug> "
"<tier>` to reflect what the spec actually is, then re-fire the nudge for "
"the new tier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:173
msgid ""
"**Container drift** (epic/initiative): declared `size:` is smaller than "
"the aggregated child rollup. Bump declared to at least the rollup tier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:177
msgid ""
"Bumping the declared field is **the lead's job**, not the engineer's. "
"Don't write code to auto-bump — surface the recommendation and let the "
"user or the lead update it via the CLI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:181
msgid "Phrasing — paste-ready"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:183
msgid ""
"These are the lines the lead should quote. Tune by tier and (where noted)"
" tracker regime. Keep them short and concrete. Don't add hedging like "
"\"you might possibly want to consider\"; say the thing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:187
msgid "`large` on feature/bug/enhancement — soft, design-time only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:189
msgid ""
"This is `large` (week+ of work). Doable as one spec, but if it spans more"
" than one subsystem consider `/split` into two specs. No action needed if"
" you're comfortable with the scope."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:193
msgid ""
"Mid-delivery for `large` is quiet — mention in handoff only if useful, "
"otherwise stay out of the way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:196
msgid "`x-large` on feature/bug/enhancement — strong, every session"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:198
msgid ""
"This is `x-large` (multi-week). Strongly recommend `/split` to break it "
"into 2–3 child specs, or `/compose` if it deserves an initiative parent. "
"Promotion creates a new initiative spec and converts this one into N "
"child specs — real overhead, but cheaper than delivering a runaway spec. "
"Want me to `/split` now?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:204
msgid ""
"Re-fire on every `/deliver` pickup. If the user says \"ship it as-is,\" "
"proceed — no `size_ack` needed for `x-large`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:207
msgid "`giant` on feature/bug/enhancement — super-strong, requires ack"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:209
msgid "Design-time and first delivery pickup:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:211
msgid ""
"This is `giant` (month+). I strongly recommend promoting to an initiative"
" with phased child specs — `/compose` will scaffold the parent and let "
"you slot child specs under it. Promotion isn't free (new parent spec, re-"
"parenting this one, writing N child specs), but a month-long single spec "
"almost always runs aground. If you want to proceed without splitting, "
"I'll stamp `size_ack: giant` in the frontmatter so I stop asking at "
"design time. Mid-delivery I'll still surface the size each session. Split"
" or ack?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:220
msgid "Mid-delivery with `size_ack: giant` set:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:222
msgid ""
"Reminder: this spec is `giant` and acknowledged. I'll proceed, but if the"
" next phase feels rough, that's the signal to `/split`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:225
msgid "Mid-delivery **without** `size_ack`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:227
msgid ""
"Still `giant` and unacknowledged. Quick decision: `/split` now, or stamp "
"`size_ack: giant` and I'll stop asking at design time (mid-delivery "
"checks continue)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:231
msgid "`large`/`x-large` on epic — light touch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:233
msgid "Epics expect to be large. Only nudge at `giant`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:235
msgid ""
"Epic is `giant` — that's bigger than an epic should carry. Recommend "
"promoting to an initiative (the next type up) and `/compose`-ing phases. "
"Want me to scaffold the initiative parent?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:239
msgid "`giant` on initiative — `/compose` recommendation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:241
msgid ""
"Initiative is `giant`. Single-pass delivery isn't realistic at this "
"scope. Strongly recommend `/compose` to break it into 3–5 sequential "
"phases, each its own deliverable child. Want me to sketch the phase "
"boundaries?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:246
msgid "Tracker-aware variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:248
msgid "When `tracker.type != \"none\"` AND `supports_hierarchy: true`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:250
msgid "Raise the trigger floor: skip the `large` soft nudge, start at `x-large`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:252
msgid "Append to the promotion ask:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:254
msgid ""
"When you split, I can also create the parent issue in <tracker> so your "
"team's tracker view matches the spec hierarchy. Want both?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:257
msgid ""
"When the tracker has no hierarchy support, fire the local-only phrasing "
"above and do not offer tracker-side parent creation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:260
msgid "What to do on drift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:262
msgid "`hero size --check` flags declared-vs-computed mismatch. The lead's move:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:265
msgid "Read the drift line. Two columns: declared tier and computed tier."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:266
msgid "**If declared is too small** (most common): bump it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:267
msgid "hero size <slug> <new-tier>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:270
msgid ""
"Then re-evaluate: the new tier may itself trigger a nudge (e.g. bumping "
"`medium` → `x-large` lands you in strong-nudge territory)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:272
msgid ""
"**If declared is too large** (rare; usually after scope shrinks): bump it"
" down. No nudge fires; the spec just looks less alarming."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:274
msgid ""
"**Container drift**: same — bump the container's declared `size:` to at "
"least match the child rollup, then check whether the new container tier "
"itself triggers a nudge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:278
msgid ""
"Don't ignore drift. The whole point of the field is to make scope changes"
" visible — ignoring drift makes `size:` lie, and a lying field is worse "
"than no field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:282
msgid "Don't block"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:284
msgid ""
"The user can override every nudge. The system records the choice (via "
"`size_ack:` for `giant`, or just by the user saying \"ship it\" for "
"`large`/`x-large`) and proceeds. Document the choice in the delivery "
"handoff so the next session sees it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:289
msgid "The nudge is a loud linter warning, not a gate. Treat it that way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:291
msgid "Composing with related skills"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:293
msgid ""
"**`spec-format`** — defines `size:` as a living frontmatter field "
"alongside `status:`. Cross-references this skill for the ladder."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:295
msgid ""
"**`agent-reliability`** — the Persistence rule applies: don't yield mid-"
"delivery just because a nudge fired. Surface the nudge, get the user's "
"call, proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:298
msgid ""
"**`kickoff-prompt`** — when rewriting a spec's `## Kickoff` after a size "
"change, reflect the new tier (and the ack state if `giant`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:300
msgid ""
"**`roadmap-review`** — the interactive triage surface for the drift this "
"skill detects. `hero size --check` reports drift; `/roadmap-review` walks"
" it one item at a time and executes the resolution CLI on confirm."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/spec-sizing/SKILL.md:303
msgid ""
"**`spec-composition`** — owns the canonical \"multiple related specs\" "
"phrasing and the multi-spec routing nudge. When a `/design` request would"
" produce N related specs (user names multiple deliverables, or the "
"rolled-up scope reaches `large`), the routing nudge from `spec-"
"composition` fires **first** — the sizing nudge stands down for that "
"moment per the precedence rule documented in that skill. Sizing nudges "
"resurface per-child after the user either pivots to `/compose` (each "
"child gets sized when its `/design` runs) or declines and proceeds with "
